      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"The Ring\"] What Hitchcock would proclaim as his second “true” film, “The Ring,” a sports-centered romance, is proof that the director doesn’t need a serial killer to carry the emotional stakes of a movie. He makes do just fine with a boxer. Following on his success with the Jack the Ripper-inspired “Lodger,” Hitchcock looks to his second passion in life (after torturing blondes) to make “The Ring;” boxing. Apparently a fervent patron of matches in London, Hitchcock has an immediate eloquence with filming fights - captured like only one who had witnessed an exceptional number of them himself. Boxing alrea",
